[NEW] &lt;p&gt;Reimagine creation Phase In/Out rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Allow users to pre-select Tables and Fields at Group level that will be populated on every rules.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;If a Table key field like Product ID is included in the rules, then auto fill related fields with values like Product Name, Product Group  (GA: January CY2027) — Dynamics 365 Supply Chain Management

[NEW] &lt;p&gt;Makers can now choose to display their data as a calendar or a stack of cards instead of the default grid layout. Makers can configure these layouts directly in the model driven app designer, giving users more intuitive ways to visualize and work with their data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Availability&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
&lt; (GA: February CY2027) — Power Apps

[DATE_CHANGED] &lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business value&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Field service work often happens in environments where network quality changes throughout the day. Technicians may move between connected, low-connectivity, intermittent, and offline conditions while still needing the mobile app to remain dependable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt; (GA: February CY2027) — Dynamics 365 Field Service

[NEW] &lt;p&gt;This release expands the contract management experience in Dynamics 365 Project Operations with:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced analytics and insights on the contract form to improve visibility into contract performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Context-based pricing information that provides additional business context  (GA: September CY2027) — Dynamics 365 Project Operations

&lt;p&gt;Real-time streaming analytics is built into the new supervisor application. An advanced streaming engine keeps metrics up to date with near-instant updates, allowing supervisors to view the latest data without refreshing the dashboard.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key capabilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continu (GA: October CY2026) — Dynamics 365 Contact Center

&lt;p&gt;Currently, to bring tasks from another project into a new project, you must manually enter the task details in the task grid or use schedule APIs. You can also use the &lt;strong&gt;Copy project&lt;/strong&gt; feature to create a new project with the same tasks, but this feature has limitations:&lt;br&gt;
​&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;u (GA: October CY2026) — Dynamics 365 Project Operations
